 ## Post-processing (external software)
 
-Microclaw produces an NDTiff dataset or a TIFF stack. The user must run
-localization fitting in one of these tools:
+Microclaw produces an NDTiff dataset or a TIFF stack, which still has to be
+fitted to localizations.
+
+**If SMAPpy is installed, call `load_skill(name="smappy")`** — it is the SMAP
+pipeline as a Python package, it reads the NDTiff dataset directly (no TIFF
+export), writes an HDF5 of localizations, and can fit while the acquisition is
+still being written. The filtering, drift-correction and grouping advice below
+applies to it unchanged; that skill has the calls.
+
+Otherwise the user runs the fit in one of these tools:
 
 | Software        | Platform    | Notes                                  |
 |-----------------|-------------|----------------------------------------|
+| SMAPpy          | Python      | SMAP's MLE pipeline as a package; 3D, live |
 | ThunderSTORM    | FIJI plugin | Widely used, good for 2D dSTORM/PALM  |
 | SMAP            | MATLAB/GUI  | State-of-art MLE, 3D, PSF calibration |
 | DECODE          | Python/GPU  | Deep-learning, very fast               |
